.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREARC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securearc
.Nd ARC chain validation and sealing milter for Postfix
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c Ar config-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a high-performance Authenticated Received Chain (ARC) milter implementing
RFC 8617.
It validates existing ARC chains on incoming mail and optionally seals
messages transiting through the mail system, preserving authentication
results across forwarding hops.
.Pp
.Nm
must be placed last in the milter chain (after SPF, DKIM, and DMARC)
so that all upstream Authentication-Results are available for inclusion
in the ARC-Authentication-Results header.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar config-file
Path to the INI-style configuration file.
Required.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses INI format with a
.Ql [global]
section and one or more
.Ql [listener:name]
sections.
.Ss Global Section
.Bl -tag -width "SyslogFacility" -compact
.It Cm AuthservID
Identifier for Authentication-Results headers.
Default:
.Dq localhost .
.It Cm LocalAuthMethods
Comma-separated list of authentication methods this ADMD evaluates locally,
for example
.Dq spf, dkim, dmarc .
When sealing, only Authentication-Results headers that claim our
.Cm AuthservID
and assert nothing outside this list are copied into the
ARC-Authentication-Results header and signed.
A host that lists no local methods has authenticated nothing, so its AAR
reports
.Dq none
rather than repeating results supplied by the sender
(RFC 8617 Section 5.1.1).
Default: empty.
.It Cm StripAuthResults
Remove every pre-existing Authentication-Results header claiming our
.Cm AuthservID ,
not just the ones asserting an
.Li arc=
result.
Enable this when
.Nm
is the first or only milter in the chain (RFC 8601 Section 5).
Default: no.
.It Cm WorkerThreads
Number of worker threads.
0 means auto-detect CPU count.
Default: 0.
.It Cm PidFile
Path to the PID file.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/securearc/securearc.pid .
.It Cm Foreground
Run in foreground without daemonizing.
Default: no.
.It Cm User
Drop privileges to this user after binding sockets.
.It Cm Syslog
Enable syslog output.
Default: yes.
.It Cm SyslogFacility
Syslog facility.
Default: mail.
.It Cm LogLevel
Logging verbosity: err, warn, info, debug.
Default: info.
.It Cm DnsNameserver
Comma-separated DNS nameserver IPs.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Cm DnsTimeout
DNS query timeout in seconds.
Default: 5.
.It Cm DnsRetries
Number of DNS query retries.
Default: 2.
.It Cm DnsCacheSize
Maximum DNS cache entries per worker.
Default: 1000.
.It Cm DnsNegativeTTL
Negative cache TTL in seconds.
Default: 60.
.It Cm SignedHeaders
Colon-separated headers included in ARC-Message-Signature.
Default:
.Dq from:to:subject:date:message-id .
.It Cm ZmqEndpoint
ZeroMQ PUB endpoint for event publishing.
Disabled if not set.
.It Cm ZmqTopic
ZeroMQ topic prefix.
Default:
.Dq arc .
.El
.Ss Listener Sections
Each
.Ql [listener:name]
section defines a socket and its operating mode.
.Bl -tag -width "SealSelector" -compact
.It Cm Socket
Listen address.
Format:
.Dq inet:port@host
or
.Dq unix:/path .
.It Cm Mode
Operating mode:
.Dq seal ,
.Dq verify ,
or
.Dq both .
Default: verify.
.It Cm SealDomain
Domain name for ARC sealing.
Required for seal mode.
.It Cm SealSelector
DNS selector for the ARC signing key.
Required for seal mode.
.It Cm SealKeyFile
Path to the private key file for ARC sealing.
Required for seal mode.
Supports RSA and Ed25519 keys in PEM format.
.El
.Pp
If no listener sections are defined, the default is
.Dq inet:8895@0.0.0.0
in verify mode.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM" -compact
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload configuration.
.It Dv SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown with 30 second drain timeout.
.El
.Sh POSTFIX INTEGRATION
.Nm
must be last in the milter chain:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
smtpd_milters = inet:127.0.0.1:8890,
                inet:127.0.0.1:8891,
                inet:127.0.0.1:8894,
                inet:127.0.0.1:8895
milter_connect_macros = j {daemon_name} v {client_addr}
milter_default_action = accept
.Ed
.Sh LOG FORMAT
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securearc[pid]: id=QUEUEID peer=HOST[IP] client=IP mode=verify|seal elapsed=Nms
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/securearc/securearc.conf"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/securearc/securearc.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /var/run/securearc/securearc.pid
Default PID file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securearc-testkey 8 ,
.Xr securespf 8 ,
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedmarc 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Authenticated Received Chain (ARC) Protocol
.%R RFC 8617
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
